But looking at the questionnaire data, it seems that some do, some don't. So when you average all the data, you do see significant differences in the amount. of dreaming, the sensory qualities of the dream. But to really understand the data, you're going to kind of dig more on an individual level where some people report they have no memory of dreams. Some people report still dreams with emotional content but less visual. Some people report sort of black and white dreams. And so there's kind of a mixture state there. But there are certainly people that have a Fantasia and do report dreaming. What about reading? I mean, if you're going to read fiction, you are going to have a mental image of what's going on in the story.

